#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

typedef void (*bc_pty_exit_cb)(int exit_code, void *userdata);

void bc_pty_on_exit(bc_client_t *c, bc_pty_exit_cb cb,
                    void *userdata);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Registers a callback function that is invoked when the PTY child process
exits.
The callback receives the child\(cqs exit code.
.PP
For normal exits, \f[B]exit_code\f[R] is the value passed to
\f[CR]exit(3)\f[R] or returned from \f[CR]main()\f[R].
For signal\-caused deaths, \f[B]exit_code\f[R] is 128 + signal number
(e.g., 137 for \f[CR]SIGKILL\f[R], 130 for \f[CR]SIGINT\f[R]).
.PP
\f[B]The callback is only invoked during \f[CB]bc_poll(3)\f[B]
calls.\f[R] The client must call \f[CR]bc_poll\f[R] regularly for exit
events to be delivered.
.PP
The exit callback fires at most once per PTY session.
After it fires, the PTY session is in a terminated state, though
\f[CR]bc_pty_close(3)\f[R] must still be called to release server\-side
resources and allow a new session to be spawned.
.PP
To unregister the callback, call
\f[CR]bc_pty_on_exit(c, NULL, NULL)\f[R].
.SH Wire protocol
Exit event arrives on \f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] (channel 5) as:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqexit\(dq,\(dqexit_code\(dq:0}
