.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The exit callback fires \f[B]before\f[R] the close acknowledgement in
\f[CR]bc_pty_close(3)\f[R].
If close triggers a kill, the sequence is: exit event callback, then
close returns \f[CR]BC_OK\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Any remaining buffered output is delivered via
\f[CR]bc_pty_on_output(3)\f[R] before the exit callback fires.
This ensures the client receives all output from the child.
.IP \(bu 2
The callback is invoked \f[B]synchronously\f[R] within
\f[CR]bc_poll(3)\f[R].
Spawning a new PTY from within the exit callback is supported but the
new session\(cqs events will not be processed until the next
\f[CR]bc_poll\f[R] call.
.IP \(bu 2
The callback registration persists across PTY close/spawn cycles.
If you close one session and spawn another, the same exit callback
applies to the new session.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: \f[CR]bc_pty_on_exit\f[R] and \f[CR]bc_poll\f[R] must be
called from the same thread.
The callback is always invoked on the thread that calls
\f[CR]bc_poll\f[R].
